⏺ This is the breakthrough. The official docs (current) describe two owner 
  self-serve commands the handoff didn't have (it was written against CLI
  v0.23.1; the local CLI is v0.9.0 and the docs have moved on):

  1. clawhub scan --slug <slug> → triggers ClawScan (re-runs SkillSpector) via
  POST /api/v1/skills/-/scan, polls to terminal; --update writes results back to
  the selected version; --output downloads the full report incl.
  skillspector.json. This is the "Rescan" the handoff couldn't find — and it's 
  CLI-driven, no dashboard/browser needed.
  2. clawhub delete <skill> --version <version> → withdraws one owned non-latest
  version specifically (not the whole skill) — a surgical way to clear the
  phantom 3.4.0. Caveat: "version number remains reserved, cannot be republished
  with different contents" — so this needs care.
  3. clawhub inspect @owner/slug (while logged in) → shows owner-visible 
  moderation diagnostics — authoritative state, including the stuck review.

